@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam ParticipantPadding 24
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #42566B
  LifeLineBorderColor #8295A8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #D8EAFE
  ActivationBorderColor #42566B
  ParticipantBorderColor #42566B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F1FA
  ParticipantFontColor #172B4D
  ActorBorderColor #42566B
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #8295A8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
  GroupHeaderFontColor #172B4D
  DividerBackgroundColor #E8F1FA
  DividerBorderColor #8295A8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
  BorderColor #BBA86A
  FontSize 12
}
hide footbox
title UC-T03 - Update Charging-Point Status
actor "External Telemetry System\n(Provider / ACT-03)" as P
boundary "Telemetry API / Adapter" as API
control "TelemetryController" as C
entity "Telemetry & Mobility Records" as D
control "Charging Scheduler" as Q
note over P,D
  What-if events must use isolated run-scoped storage.
end note
P -> API: Submit event (point/Hub, eventRef, observedAt, condition; session/vehicle and measurements when required)
activate API
API -> C: Process event with source credentials and operational/run scope
activate C
C -> D: Read provider permissions, resource scope and validation policy
activate D
D --> C: Policy / unavailable
deactivate D
C -> C: Verify source identity, resource authorization and operational/run scope
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
alt policy unavailable
C -> C: Set retryable failure; no operational update
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else source or scope unauthorized
C -> D: Record access failure without protected resource details
activate D
D --> C: Audit recorded / audit unavailable
deactivate D
C -> C: Set access denied; never apply event
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else authorized source and scope
C -> C: Validate point/Hub mapping, event type, timestamp, supported\nstate and required session/vehicle/progress/stop references
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
alt invalid event / unknown mapping
C -> C: Set validation rejection; retain last accepted state and freshness
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else structurally valid
C -> D: Read original event result/fingerprint and latest accepted observation\nfor this resource/reporting scope (and session when applicable)
activate D
D --> C: Prior result and observation / unavailable
deactivate D
alt event state unavailable
C -> C: Set retryable failure; do not infer availability
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else identical event already processed
C -> C: Use original result; do not advance freshness or repeat effects
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else identity conflict, stale or out-of-order event
C -> D: Retain conflicting evidence where applicable; do not alter accepted observation
activate D
D --> C: Evidence result / unavailable
deactivate D
C -> C: Set rejection reason; do not reset freshness
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else new event satisfies ordering and freshness rules
loop initial attempt; repeat only after concurrency conflict while retry policy permits
C -> D: Read current point restrictions, Hub state, schedule, session/request, vehicle and private-EV parking context\nand versions in the selected scope
activate D
D --> C: Consistent context / unavailable
deactivate D
alt context unavailable
C -> C: Set retryable failure; stop this retry loop
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else context available
C -> C: Match session to point/vehicle; validate transition and allocation
activate C
C --> C: Compatible transition / unresolved report
deactivate C
alt session mismatch or incompatible transition
C -> C: Plan unresolved evidence for Operator reconciliation;\nunexpected start blocks new allocations pending verification
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else compatible observation
  alt confirmed start / progress
C -> C: Start requires valid allocation, operational Hub/point;\nprivate EV requires Active parking + Checked In reservation;\nmark existing session/request Active or update progress without restarting
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
  else confirmed stop / completion / permitted pause
C -> C: Completed if target met; Interrupted for final stop before target;\nPaused only under session policy; retain actual time;\nrelease only capacity no longer committed, once
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
  else condition-only report (healthy, idle or fault)
C -> C: Update reported condition; preserve open restrictions and future allocations
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
  end
end
opt validated point fault, including fault accompanying a session report
C -> C: Restrict point; create/update equivalent incident; identify affected allocations;\nwithout confirmed cessation retain last confirmed session state and require verification
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
end
critical Final event identity, ordering and business-state check + atomic update
C -> D: Atomically commit observation/effects and original processing result only if\nidentity, order, permissions and context versions still match;\npersist scheduling work for eligible capacity release
activate D
note right of D
  Unresolved transitions save evidence, not a valid session transition.
end note
D --> C: Committed / original duplicate result / stale or conflicting /\nconcurrency conflict / failed / outcome unknown
deactivate D
end
C -> C: Retry only concurrency conflicts with a fresh context;\notherwise stop loop and classify result
activate C
C --> C: Retry / terminal outcome
deactivate C
end
end
opt outcome unknown
C -> D: Find original processing result using same source, scope and eventRef
activate D
D --> C: Original applied/rejected/failed result / not yet resolved
deactivate D
end
opt newly committed observation/evidence (including recovered commit)
C -> C: Expose accepted time, freshness, restrictions and discrepancies\nfrom committed records to monitoring/detail views
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
end
opt committed eligible capacity release has pending scheduling work
C -> Q: Signal scoped durable work (eventRef); re-evaluate eligible queue
activate Q
Q -> D: Claim work idempotently and use current capacity/policy
activate D
D --> Q: Work/context or already handled / unavailable
deactivate D
Q --> C: Accepted / already handled / retry pending
deactivate Q
note over C,Q
  Failed notification leaves scheduling work pending.
  A pause alone does not prove free capacity.
end note
end
end
end
end
C --> API: Processing result + event reference (applied / original / rejected / retryable / unresolved)
deactivate C
alt acknowledgement delivered
API --> P: Return processing result; unknown is not an applied acknowledgement
else acknowledgement lost
API -> API: Response delivery fails; committed result is retained
activate API
API --> API: Provider may retry same event identity and payload
deactivate API
end
deactivate API
note over P,D
  Charging telemetry does not close parking.
end note
footer Smart E-Mobility Hub | Submission 2 | External Telemetry
@enduml
